+### Request routing inside the wrapped client
+
+| Call | Handled locally when | Otherwise |
+|---|---|---|
+| `fetchQuote`, `fetchIndicativeQuote` | Both chain ids are 1301 and the pair is USDC <-> a registered (or on-chain resolvable) outcome token. Returns a CLASSIC quote with `gasFee`, 1-hop `v4-pool` route and, when the Permit2 -> UR allowance is missing, `permitData` (or `permitTransaction` with `generatePermitAsTransaction`) | Hosted API. An outcome token paired with anything but USDC throws 404 |
+| `fetchCheckApproval` | 1301 and `token` or `tokenOut` is an outcome token. Checks ERC20 -> Permit2 and returns `approve(Permit2, max)` + `gasFee` | Hosted API |
+| `fetchSwap` | The echoed quote is a 1301 USDC <-> outcome pair. Rebuilds calldata with the signed permit; `simulateTransaction` runs `eth_estimateGas` (limit x1.2) and throws on revert. Without it (the app does not simulate until approvals are done, i.e. the first buy) the limit is max(1,000,000, 2 x quoted gas + 100k): Unichain charges only gas used | Hosted API |
+| `fetchSwaps` | Any 1301 tx hash: `SUCCESS`/`FAILED` from the receipt, `PENDING` if none yet | Hosted API |
+| `fetchCheckPermissions` | 1301 and any token is an outcome token: all `isPermissioned: false` | Hosted API |
+| `fetchSwap5792`, `fetchSwap7702`, `fetchSwap4337` | Our quote: throw 404 with an explanation | Hosted API |
