+## 7. Price chart for YES/NO tokens
+
+The swap page's chart toggle (trending icon, desktop widths) opens the slideout price card. For a YES/NO token the card
+charts the hook's own quotes instead of Uniswap's backend history.
+
+- History is rebuilt exactly from chain state: `hook.quote(marketId)` with `eth_call` at each past block, from `openTime`
+  up to the last second the hook prices (`expiry - window - 1`; inside the averaging window `midYes` is 0). Each point's
+  time is `expiry - tau` from the quote itself. A 60 s market is at most 50 points; longer markets are sampled to 240
+  points on a grid anchored at `openTime`, so the grid does not move between refreshes.
+- YES plots `midYes`, NO plots `1 - midYes`, in USD. Once the market is settled the line ends at `expiry` with 1.00 for
+  the winner and 0.00 for the loser (0.50 for an invalid market). Between `expiry - window` and settlement the line
+  holds its last quote.
+- While the card is open it polls once per second: one multicall at `latest` (quote, `marketInfo`, block number and
+  timestamp), plus reads of any block it missed. Past reads are cached per market for the page's lifetime (32 markets)
+  and shared by YES and NO. Polling stops when the market is settled and its history is complete, or the card closes.
+- drpc's free tier rejects JSON-RPC batches above 3 calls, so history reads are single `eth_call`s, 6 at a time.
+  Measured in Chrome on `localhost:3000`: a finished 60 s market loads in about 1.3 s, a live one in about 0.9 s, and each
+  later poll takes about 130 ms.
+- The card defaults to the YES/NO side of a USDC <-> YES/NO pair, hides the 1H-1Y selector and the expand button (there
+  is no token details page for these tokens), shows seconds in the crosshair time and skips the low-variance y-axis
+  zoom. Every other token keeps the backend data and the stock card.
+
