+## 10. Market tracks (MarketGatekeeper)
+
+The hook's owner is a `MarketGatekeeper` that forwards `createMarket` from a fixed set of `MarketScheduler`s, one per
+track (asset, cadence and market length). The planned tracks are ETH1M, ETH15M, SOL1M and SOL15M, each with its own
+oracle. The fork reads them like this:
+
+- **Deployment.** `getPredictionDeployment()` adds `marketGatekeeper`, `marketSchedulers` and `underlyings`
+  (`{symbol, token, oracle}`) to the vendored SDK's fields (`parseTracksDeployment` in `config.ts`). Without
+  `underlyings` there is one ETH entry built from `underlyingOracle` and `demoWeth`. Without `marketSchedulers` the old
+  single `marketScheduler` is the only track. A `prediction.hook` override other than the file's hook has no tracks.
+- **Tracks.** Read once per page from `gatekeeper.schedulers()` (the file's list when there is no gatekeeper), then
+  `config()` and `oracle()` per scheduler. The asset is the `underlyings` symbol behind the track's oracle, else the
+  ticker without its period suffix. The label is "ETH 1-minute" (market length from `tenor`). Tracks are ordered by
+  asset in first-seen order, then by period.
+- **Classification.** A market's track is `gatekeeper.schedulerOf(id)`, read once per id in the registry poll's
+  extra multicall. Without a gatekeeper, or for an id it never created, the track whose ticker gives the outcome
+  symbol exactly (`ticker + "UP"` or `ticker + "DOWN"`); never a prefix, since "ETH" is a prefix of "ETH15M".
+- **Recent markets per track.** Each registry poll also reads `scheduler.marketOfSlot(slot)` for the current slot and
+  the 2 before it on every track (the same multicall). Ids outside the newest-40 window are read with
+  `readPredictionMarketsByIds` until they settle, so the 15-minute markets are not pushed out by the 1-minute ones.
+- **Picker.** `selectPredictionMarketsForPicker` groups open markets by track (up to 4 per track) and takes the 2 newest
+  settled markets of every track, newest expiry first. The clock ticks every second while a track of 2 minutes or less
+  exists. Markets no track claims go to "Other prediction markets"; with no tracks at all the picker falls back to one
+  "Prediction markets" section, as before.
+- **Full symbols.** `getCurrencySymbolDisplayText` (`symbolDisplay.ts`) returns the whole symbol of a registered
+  outcome token and the stock 6-character cut for anything else. Used by the token selector row
+  (`BaseTokenOptionItem`) and the swap form token button (`SelectTokenButton`). Other places (review screen, balances,
+  activity) still cut, so "ETH15MDOWN" reads "ETH15…" there.
+- **Market panel.** The question names the market's asset ("SOL above $151.20 at 14:15:00 UTC?") and the facts line
+  starts with the track's length ("15-minute market"). The spot price comes from the market's own oracle
+  (`marketInfo.oracle`): the registry's copy when the market is registered, else learned on the first read and
+  remembered per market. There is no deployment-wide ETH oracle fallback any more.
